<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- TemporalPaneForeCastContent — the CONTENT of the ForeCast window: the SPC outlook (card + day / product / opacity) with
     its legend, plus NowCast's GHOST rows around it. One of three mode Contents (see Controls/TemporalPanes/TemporalPane,
     registered once per mode); the window supplies the surface, the title and the pin, so this is content only.
     Named as the tree reads (TemporalPane → TemporalPaneForeCastContent). Bound to the coordinator
     MapViewModel; every real control here drives ViewModel.Outlook.

       ┌──┐ ForeCast                    │ MDT 4/5                  ← THE NAME ROW (Past/Now's, matched): square =
       │██│ Day 1 · Wed Sep 2           │ next ~9 min                the HIGHEST category in the shown outlook, in
       └──┘                                                          its SPC colour (blue = no areas); readout =
                                                                     that category + the refresh countdown
       [x] Show NowCast ghost rows                               ← persisted, default off; fixed (doesn't scroll)
       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ ⠿   ░░ ░Storm cells · NowCast░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ │  ← GHOSTS (DragMoveLayerExpander IsGhost): NowCast's
       │ ⠿   ░░ ░Warnings · NowCast░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ │     layers, 25%, drag-only — only while the
       │ …                                                    │     box is on AND NowCast runs. ONE shared
       │ ⠿ ⌄ [x] SPC outlook  ────────●──────   55%           │     Now + Fore order: a drag here moves
       │                                                      │     NowCast's window too, and vice versa
       │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐        │
       │  │ Day 1 · Categorical                      │        │  the card: which outlook is
       │  │ Issued 12:57 PM · Valid → Wed 7:00 AM    │        │  drawn, when SPC issued it,
       │  │ Next ~9 min                              │        │  and the refresh countdown
       │  └──────────────────────────────────────────┘        │
       │  [Day 1 · Wed Sep 2    ▾] [Categorical          ▾]  │  ← COMPACT, no row labels (the user's call, 2026-10-28):
       │  [‹][1630Z (Latest)  ▾][›]           [Discussion.]  │     ONE grid: col 0 (212) = Day ≡ ‹ Cycle › (same width,
       │  ↑ col 0 edges line up ↑                             │     aligned) | col 1 = Product ≡ Discussion. (flush right);
       │                                                      │     ‹ ›
       │  2 of 3 today · 06Z · 13Z · 1630Z [✓] Prev. outline │     stepping the list (ends grey) … Discussion. opens the
       │                                                      │     Outlook Discussion WINDOW. Cycle = today's earlier
       │                                                      │     issuances (HELD) | the newest = the live feed, tagged;
       │                                                      │     the box draws the cycle BEFORE the drawn one dashed
       │  ›  Legend ──────────────────────────────────────    │  ← the LEGEND (Primitives/OutlookLegend), a minimal FOLD
       │   ■ 2%              Opacity ──────●────── 80%       │     (folded by default, "fore/outlook-legend"). Open:
       │   ■ 5%              Intensity hatching   [✓] Show    │     LAST in the section body, so it goes
       │   ■ 10%             ╱ CIG1             In Outlook    │     with the section when collapsed; also
       │   ■ 15%             ╲ CIG2             In Outlook    │     hidden when HasLegend is false (None).
       │   ■ 30%             ╳ CIG3         Not In Outlook    │
       │                                                      │  ← colours | hatching, two equal halves; the
       │                                                      │     hatching half only when the product has
       │                                                      │     intensity groups (status from the CACHED GeoJSON)
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
       │ ⠿ ⌄ [x] Short Range      ─────────●───────   80%  │  ← the forecast MODEL (DragMoveLayerExpanderShortRangeBody):
       │   ▓ HRRR 16Z · all 18 hours in    Next 18 hr · CAM ▓│     card (range note right) · frame line · Model · Product ·
       │   valid 11:00 PM (f05:00)                            │     Run · Tracks (UH) · Hours; its legend is in the pane notches.
       │   Model [HRRR]  Product […▾]  Run [Latest▾] …        │     ⚠️ ticked + ForeCast on = NowCast OFF (and back on
       │                                                      │     when unticked) — MapViewModel's NowCast ⇄ MODEL
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
       │ ⠿   ░░ ░Radar · NowCast░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░ │  ← ghost (default spot: under the model)
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                                             ┃  ← all of the above sits in PanelScroller: a 16 px
                                                                gutter always claimed, thumb ┃ only on overflow

     ONE REAL SECTION, a TemporalPanes/DragMoveLayerExpanders/DragMoveLayerExpander (every temporal window's map-layer section). SPC outlook
     is open on a first run — it is what the window is for. Open/closed is then PERSISTED ("fore/..." in
     AppSettings.SectionExpanded; ghosts don't persist — they have no body), and so are Day, Product, opacity
     and hatching (ViewModels/Map/TemporalWindowPersistence). Inside it: a summary CARD, then [label | control]
     rows in one aligned 60px column, then the legend.
     ⚠️ The window opens at a FIXED full height, so the layer run SCROLLS inside Primitives/PanelScroller
     (2026-09-30, the same scroller as Past/Now). WinUI's bar is not wanted — see the PanelScroller header.
     ⚠️ THE DISCUSSION IS A WINDOW NOW (Windows/OutlookDiscussionWindow, the Product row's "Discussion."). It
     was an inline collapsed section pinned at the bottom of this body until 2026-10-01 (the user's call).

     ⚠️ THE OUTLOOK HEADER'S BOX IS A LAYER SHOW/HIDE (OutlookViewModel.IsShown), NOT the mode. The mode is
     OutlookViewModel.IsOutlookVisible (MapViewModel.IsForeCast projects onto it), and a tab body never arms
     or clears its own mode — see the last ⚠️ in this header. The box sits UNDER the mode, exactly as
     PastCast's outlook box does.
     ⚠️ GHOST ROWS: ForeCast has no layer order of its own — its outlook lives in the SHARED Now + Fore order
     (MapViewModel's GHOST ROWS block; saved as NowCastLayerOrder). The ghosts are NowCast's layers in the map's
     default spots (LayerOrder.Default); a drag here saves the Now order and the NowCast window follows
     (LayerOrderChanged). A ghost's box mirrors the real show/hide, inert.

     ⚠️ THE CARD COSTS NO VIEW-MODEL WORK. Its three lines are OutlookViewModel state that was already
     being computed and shown nowhere — the title, the issued/valid line, and the refresh countdown. See
     the card region in that class.

     ⚠️ THE LEGEND LIVES INSIDE THE OUTLOOK SECTION, last, exactly as in PastCast (both host the shared
     Primitives/OutlookLegend). It used to be its own star row outside the section; the user's call
     (2026-09-28) was one shape for both windows, so collapsing the section now takes the legend with it.
     The Day row is the same ComboBox in both windows too.

     ⚠️ THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO REAL RADAR SECTION HERE, unlike Past and Now (the radar row is a GHOST,
     inert). Radar opacity is a GLOBAL value, and those two windows can only get away with sharing a control
     for it because their modes are mutually exclusive. ForeCast COEXISTS with NowCast, so a live slider here
     would be a second control writing the same value with both windows on screen.

     ⚠️ Opacity is DISABLED while Product is None or the box hides it (ShownOnMap) — the same rule the
     PastCast outlook and the storm-report dots follow.

     ⚠️ This tab does NOT turn ForeCast on or off; that is the ForeCast key in the bottom bar's centre
     cluster. A tab body configures a mode, the key runs it. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.TemporalPanes.TemporalPaneContents.TemporalPaneForeCastContent"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:tp="using:Anvil.Controls.TemporalPanes"
             xmlns:temporalPaneHeaderReadouts="using:Anvil.Controls.TemporalPanes.TemporalPaneHeaderReadouts"
             xmlns:temporalPaneContents="using:Anvil.Controls.TemporalPanes.TemporalPaneContents"
             xmlns:dragMoveLayerExpanders="using:Anvil.Controls.TemporalPanes.DragMoveLayerExpanders"
             xmlns:conv="using:Anvil.Converters"
             xmlns:local="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:models="using:Anvil.Models"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             xmlns:layout="using:Anvil.Layout"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <conv:BoolToVisibilityConverter x:Key="BoolToVis"/>
        <conv:HexToBrushConverter x:Key="HexToBrush"/>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <!-- ⚠️ NOT top-aligned, unlike the Past/Now roots: TemporalPane hands this the full window height, and
         the star row is the SCROLLER, which fills it. -->
    <Grid x:Name="Root">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- THE NAME ROW: square · ForeCast over the day │ highest risk -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- "Show NowCast ghost rows" -->
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>    <!-- the layer run in PanelScroller: fills the space, scrolls when it can't -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- ===================== THE NAME ROW: TemporalPanes/TemporalPaneHeader (one control, all three windows) =====================
             The window's chrome carries no title any more (TemporalPane); the name shows once, here. The header
             owns its height.
             ⚠️ THE SQUARE = the HIGHEST category the shown outlook contains, in its SPC colour (DATA, never themed —
             the feed's own fill, else the catalog's), as NowCast's square is the warnings feed's staleness. No areas
             / nothing shown = PastCast's blue (OutlookViewModel.NoAreasFill). Its tooltip names the category.
             ⚠️ Margin LEFT 0 / RIGHT 4 = the section stack's edges — PastCast's + NowCast's rule; change together.
             No TemporalHeaderMinHeight: there are no tiles or card under it to line up. -->
        <tp:TemporalPaneHeader x:Name="TemporalPaneHeader" Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,12,4,12"
                                   Title="ForeCast"
                                   StatusFill="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HeaderSquareFill, Mode=OneWay, Converter={StaticResource HexToBrush}}"
                                   StatusToolTip="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HeaderSquareTip, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   Subtitle="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HeaderDayText, Mode=OneWay}">
            <temporalPaneHeaderReadouts:TemporalPaneHeaderForeCastReadout x:Name="TemporalPaneHeaderForeCastReadout"
                                                       ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </tp:TemporalPaneHeader>

        <!-- GHOST ROWS box: NowCast's layers as dimmed, drag-only rows around the outlook, so you can say where the
             outlook draws among them (ONE shared Now + Fore order). Persisted, default off; the rows show only
             while NowCast runs too (MapViewModel's GHOST ROWS block). -->
        <CheckBox x:Name="ShowNowCastGhostRowsCheckBox" Grid.Row="1" Margin="0,0,0,8" Content="Show NowCast ghost rows"
                  IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShowNowCastGhostRows, Mode=TwoWay}"
                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="List NowCast's layers here, dimmed, so you can drag the outlook among them (shown while NowCast is on)"/>

        <!-- ===================== THE LAYER RUN: one contiguous block of layer sections ===================== -->
        <!-- ⚠️ In Primitives/PanelScroller, like Past/Now's sections — present whether or not the outlook overflows
             yet (the user's call, 2026-09-30): the gutter is always claimed, the thumb only draws on overflow.
             Margin right -12 BLEEDS the gutter into the window's 16 px body margin (the PanelScroller header).
             ⚠️ A TemporalPanes/DragMoveLayerExpanders/DragMoveLayerExpanderHost of its own (like Past/Now's): the outlook + NowCast's ghost
             rows. With the ghosts hidden the outlook is alone, so its grip shows but a drag never starts
             (the host needs 2 visible). Reordered → SetLayerOrder(Now): the shared Now + Fore order. -->
        <prim:PanelScroller Grid.Row="2" Margin="0,0,-12,0">
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpanderHost x:Name="DragMoveLayerExpanderHost" VerticalAlignment="Top" Spacing="8" Margin="{StaticResource TemporalListEndClearance}" Reordered="OnLayersReordered">

        <!-- ===================== GHOSTS: NowCast's layers, in the map's default spots ===================== -->
        <!-- Drag-only (IsGhost); boxes mirror the real show/hides, inert. Collapsed = still in the run, so the
             saved order keeps their places. The XAML order IS the map default (LayerOrder.Default). -->
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander Header="Storm cells · NowCast" LayerId="cells"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormCells.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander Header="Storm reports · NowCast" LayerId="reports"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander Header="Warnings · NowCast" LayerId="warnings"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Warnings.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander Header="Watches · NowCast" LayerId="watches"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Watches.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander Header="Mesoscale discussions · NowCast" LayerId="mds"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Discussions.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>

        <!-- ===================== SPC OUTLOOK: the card, then the selectors ===================== -->
        <!-- LayerId → the grip. The header box is SHOW/HIDE (Outlook.IsShown, persisted) — NOT the mode, which
             is the bottom bar's ForeCast key; hiding keeps Day / Product. Works whatever the product, None
             included (PastCast's rule). Opacity greys while hidden or None: nothing drawn to fade. -->
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander x:Name="OutlookSection" Header="SPC outlook" LayerId="outlook" IsExpanded="True"
                          
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.IsShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnOutlookHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Show or hide the outlook (keeps the day and product you picked)"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.OutlookOpacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.ShownOnMap, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Outlook fill opacity (outlines stay solid)">
            <Grid>
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the card (its bottom edge is the rule) -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the selectors -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- the legend: last, so a collapsed section takes it along -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <!-- THE CARD, the same shape as the PastCast outlook's and for the same reason: it is a
                     RESULT, not a preview — there is no Load here, the outlook applies the moment you pick it,
                     so it describes what is on the map right now. That is also why it carries no button. -->
                <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpanderHeaderCard Grid.Row="0"
                        Headline="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CardHeadline, Mode=OneWay}"
                        Context="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CardContext, Mode=OneWay}"
                        Footer="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CardFooter, Mode=OneWay}"/>

                <!-- THE SELECTORS, COMPACT (the user's call, 2026-10-28): NO row labels — Day self-labels, the rest
                     carry tooltips. Row 0 = Day (narrowed) | Product; row 1 = ‹ Cycle › … Discussion.; row 2 = where
                     the step is + the Previous outline box. -->
                <!-- ⚠️ ONE GRID, TWO COLUMNS SHARED BY BOTH ROWS (the user's call, 2026-10-28): the Day box and the
                     ‹ Cycle › group are the SAME width (column 0) and align vertically; Product and Discussion. share
                     column 1. Resize = the one column width. -->
                <Grid Grid.Row="1" RowSpacing="8" ColumnSpacing="8">
                    <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="212"/>
                        <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Day | Product -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- ‹ Cycle › | Discussion. -->
                        <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Cycle position + Previous outline -->
                    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                    <!-- Day: self-labeling ("Day 1 · Sat Jun 14"); changing it cascades the product list. NARROWED to
                         its longest label so Product fits beside it.
                         ⚠️ A ComboBox in BOTH windows (PastCast's Day row matches): the live outlook runs to
                         EIGHT days (d4-8 are the extended probabilistic), well past what a SegmentedPicker
                         suits, and one control keeps the two sections identical.
                         Product: the day's outlook types (+ None). The list CASCADES with the day, so it stays
                         a dropdown — its length changes. -->
                    <ComboBox x:Name="OutlookDayComboBox" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.Days}"
                              DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                              SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.SelectedDayOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="SPC outlook day"/>
                    <ComboBox x:Name="OutlookProductComboBox" Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                              ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.ProductOptions, Mode=OneWay}"
                              DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                              SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.SelectedOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Outlook product (None clears the overlay)"/>

                    <!-- Cycle: Latest = the live feed, following every new issuance; an earlier one of today's is
                         fetched from IEM and HELD. Not persisted (see OutlookViewModel). Disabled while None, or when
                         the day has nothing earlier to pick (days 4-8, or before the first issuance). ‹ › step the
                         SAME list (the user's call, 2026-10-28) so a step is exactly a pick; each end greys. The group
                         fills column 0, so its edges line up with the Day box above. "Discussion." (opens the Outlook
                         Discussion window) sits in column 1, flush right. -->
                    <Grid Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" ColumnSpacing="4">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <Button x:Name="OutlookCycleBackButton" Padding="8,5" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CanStepCycleBack, Mode=OneWay}"
                                Click="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.StepCycleBack}"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Previous issuance"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Previous issuance">
                            <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE76B;" FontSize="12"/>
                        </Button>
                        <ComboBox x:Name="OutlookCycleComboBox" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CanPickCycle, Mode=OneWay}"
                                  ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CycleOptions, Mode=OneWay}"
                                  DisplayMemberPath="Label"
                                  SelectedItem="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.SelectedCycleOption, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="SPC issuance (UTC); Latest follows each new one, an earlier one stays put"/>
                        <Button x:Name="OutlookCycleForwardButton" Grid.Column="2" Padding="8,5" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                                IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CanStepCycleForward, Mode=OneWay}"
                                Click="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.StepCycleForward}"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Next issuance"
                                ToolTipService.ToolTip="Next issuance">
                            <FontIcon Glyph="&#xE76C;" FontSize="12"/>
                        </Button>
                    </Grid>
                    <Button x:Name="OutlookDiscussionButton" Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                            Content="Discussion."
                            IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HasOutlook, Mode=OneWay}"
                            Click="OnDiscussionClick"
                            ToolTipService.ToolTip="Read SPC's forecast discussion for this outlook in its own window"/>

                    <!-- Where the step is ("2 of 3 today · 06Z · 13Z · 1630Z") + the PREVIOUS-issuance outline box
                         (persisted, default on): the cycle before the drawn one, dashed on the map. -->
                    <Grid Grid.Row="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" ColumnSpacing="8"
                          Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CanPickCycle, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVis}, Mode=OneWay}">
                        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                            <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.CyclePositionText, Mode=OneWay}"
                                   VerticalAlignment="Center" FontSize="12" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
                        <CheckBox x:Name="ShowPreviousIssuanceCheckBox" Grid.Column="1" Content="Previous outline" MinWidth="0"
                                  IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.ShowPreviousCycle, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                  ToolTipService.ToolTip="Outline the issuance before this one (dashed) to see how the areas moved"/>
                    </Grid>
                </Grid>

                <!-- THE LEGEND: last in the body. Hides on HasLegend (None, or the layer off); the section's
                     own collapse hides it with everything else. -->
                <prim:OutlookLegend Grid.Row="2"
                                    Visibility="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HasLegend, Converter={StaticResource BoolToVis}, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    Entries="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.LegendEntries, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    HatchRows="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HatchLegendRows, Mode=OneWay}"
                                    ShowHatching="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.ShowHatching, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                    HatchOpacity="{x:Bind ViewModel.Outlook.HatchOpacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                    Loaded="OnOutlookLegendLoaded"
                                    ExpandedChanged="OnOutlookLegendExpandedChanged"/>
            </Grid>
        </dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander>

        <!-- ===================== SHORT RANGE: a convection-allowing model (the HRRR) ===================== -->
        <!-- LayerId "models" (layers.js GROUPS ⇄ LayerOrder.ModelField). The box is SHOW/HIDE AND THE NOWCAST SWITCH:
             while it draws, live radar is off (MapViewModel's NowCast ⇄ MODEL rule). Medium / Long Range join here
             when built (ONE box ticked at a time across them). Opacity greys while it isn't drawing. -->
        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander x:Name="DragMoveLayerExpanderShortRange" Header="Short Range"
                           LayerId="models"
                           ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange.IsShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                           CheckBoxClick="OnShortRangeHeaderClick"
                           CheckBoxToolTip="Draw the model on the map (turns NowCast's live radar off while it's on)"
                           ShowOpacity="True"
                           OpacityValue="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange.Opacity, Mode=TwoWay}"
                           IsOpacityEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange.IsDrawing, Mode=OneWay}"
                           OpacityToolTip="Model field opacity">
            <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpanderShortRangeBody x:Name="DragMoveLayerExpanderShortRangeBody"
                                                                        ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.ShortRange}"/>
        </dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander>

        <dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpander Header="Radar · NowCast" LayerId="radar"
                           IsGhost="True" ShowCheckBox="True"
                           IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowRadarLayer, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Visibility="{x:Bind GhostVisibility(ViewModel.AreNowCastGhostsShown), Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </dragMoveLayerExpanders:DragMoveLayerExpanderHost>
        </prim:PanelScroller>
        <!-- (The inline "Forecast discussion" section that sat pinned below here is GONE — SPC's discussion
             moved to its own window, the Outlook Discussion window, opened by the Product row's "Discussion."
             button. The user's call, 2026-10-01.) -->
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
